Agile helps teams build the right software.

DevOps helps teams deliver and operate that software efficiently.

Simple Analogy

Imagine building a house.

Agile

The architect and builders work together to design and construct the house in phases.

DevOps

Once the house is built, utilities, security systems, maintenance, monitoring, and ongoing support are put in place.

Agile focuses on creating.

DevOps focuses on delivering and maintaining.

