Key Takeaways
Agile focuses on planning, developing, and iterating on software.
DevOps focuses on automating delivery, deployment, operations, and monitoring.
Agile and DevOps complement each other rather than compete.
In modern organizations, Agile + DevOps together enable faster, more reliable software delivery.
